{"name":"Buttered Rum","hex":"#9d702e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"buttered","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of butter"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Spread with butter.","Of a turn, achieved by the buttering action."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buttered"},{"term":"rum","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2/B language code for Romanian."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A spirit distilled from various preparations of sugarcane, particularly fermented cane sugar and molasses.","A serving of rum."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rum"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hot buttered rum","blocks":[{"text":"Hot buttered rum is a mixed drink containing rum, butter, hot water or cider, a sweetener, and various spices. It is especially popular in the fall and winter and is traditionally associated with the holiday season. In the United States, hot buttered rum dates back to colonial days. During that time many families had their own recipes, and early Americans believed rum to be nutritious and a strengthener of the body."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Hot_buttered_rum_-_close-up.jpg/330px-Hot_buttered_rum_-_close-up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_buttered_rum","wikidata":"Q11337807"},{"title":"Butter","blocks":[{"text":"Butter is a dairy product made from the fat and protein components of churned cream. It is a semi-solid emulsion at room temperature, consisting of approximately 81% butterfat. It is used at room temperature as a spread, melted as a condiment, and used as a fat in baking, sauce-making, pan frying, and other cooking procedures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/%C5%A0v%C3%A9dsk%C3%BD_kol%C3%A1%C4%8D_naruby_904_%28cropped%29.JPG/330px-%C5%A0v%C3%A9dsk%C3%BD_kol%C3%A1%C4%8D_naruby_904_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butter","wikidata":"Q34172"},{"title":"Rum","blocks":[{"text":"Rum is a liquor made by fermenting and then distilling sugarcane molasses or sugarcane juice. The distillate, initially a clear liquid, is often aged in barrels. Rum originated in the Caribbean in the 17th century, where it was likely first created by enslaved people on sugar plantations, but has come to be produced in nearly every major sugar-producing region of the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/A_glass_of_rum.jpg/330px-A_glass_of_rum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rum","wikidata":"Q83376"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Hot_buttered_rum.jpg/500px-Hot_buttered_rum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Hot_buttered_rum.jpg/500px-Hot_buttered_rum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hot buttered rum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHot_buttered_rum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Buttered_crumpet3.jpg/500px-Buttered_crumpet3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Buttered_crumpet3.jpg/1280px-Buttered_crumpet3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Buttered_crumpet3.jpg/500px-Buttered_crumpet3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Butter spread on a crumpet using a butter knife","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AButtered_crumpet3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thum